   {
    "member": "Chip Roy",
    "speaker_label": "MR. ROY",
    "transcript": "THANK YOU, BRIAN. THANK YOU FOR YOUR STEADFAST LEADERSHOP AND PREPSHIP. APPRECIATE YOU. I'M GOING TO INVITE ANOTHER FRIEND OF MINE, NO STRANGER TO FLOODS, MY FRIEND RANDY WEBER. AS HE COMES UP TO THE MICROPHONE I WANT TO POINT OUT THE EXTENT TO WHICH THIS DELEGATION, I KNOW IS GRATEFULLER IN LEADERSHIP OF OUR GOVERN YORK GOVERNOR ABBOTT, OF THED OF THE TEXAS DEPARTMENT OF EMERGENCY MANAGEMENT, OF THE COUNTLESS INDIVIDUALS AND PUBLIC SERVANTS AFFILIATE WITH THE DEPARTMENT OF PUBLIC SAFETY, ITS HEAD, FREEMAN MARTIN. THE FOLKS ASSOCIATED WITH THE SHERIFF'S DEPARTMENT IN KERR COUNTY, THROUGHOUT THE REGION, OTHER AREAS A.F.C.KED BY FLOODS, THE CITY MANAGER IN KERRVILLE HAS DONE A FANTASTIC JOB. WE'VE JUST HAD SO MUCH FANTASTIC LEADERSHIP OF PEOPLE IN THE STATE OF TEXAS STEPPING UP AND AS BRIAN SAID SO MANY VOLUNTEERS FROM ACROSS THE STATE. WE CONTINUE TO, I WANT TO BE VERY CLEAR, ALL OF THIS IS CURRENT. PRESIDENT. THE SEARCH CONTINUES. CONTINUES TODAY. THEY'RE ENGAGE RIGHT NOW. AND WE'RE DEEPLY APPRECIATIVE FOR IT. WITH THAT, I'D LIKE TO YIELD THREE MINUTES TO MY GOOD FRIEND, RANDY WEBER.",
    "topic": "elections_government",
