   {
    "member": "Chip Roy",
    "speaker_label": "MR. ROY",
    "transcript": "I THANK THE SPEAKER. EARLIER TODAY I ROSE TO LEAD THE TEXAS DELEGATION, MY FRIENDS AND THIS ENTIRE BODY IN A MOMENT OF SILENCE FOR ALL OF THOSE WHO HAVE BEEN AFFECTED BY THE FLOOD IN TEXAS AND PARTICULARLY THOSE THAT WERE AFFECTED IN THE DISTRICT IN WHICH I'M PROUD TO REPRESENT IN CENTRAL TEXAS. IT HAS ALWAYS BEEN AN HONOR, AS I OFTEN SAY OUT ON THE CAMPAIGN TRAIL, TO REPRESENT THE BEST PART OF THE BEST STATE OF THE BEST COUNTRY IN THE HISTORY OF THE WORLD AND THAT PARTICULAR PART OF THE STATE IS, AS ONE OF MY STAFFERS DESCRIBE IT, HEAVEN ON EARTH. AT LEAST THAT'S HOW MANY OF US HAVE VIEWED IT HISTORICALLY. AND IT IS A REASON WHY THERE HAVE BEEN FOR NOW A CENTURY MULTIPLE CAMPS FOR CHILDREN ALONG THIS BEAUTIFUL PART OF THE TEXAS HILL COUNTRY, THE CENTERPIECE OF WHICH IS THE GUADALUPE RIVER. AND THOSE PEOPLE WHO LIVE ALONG IT CHERISH IT. THOSE PEOPLE WHO GO THERE FOR CAMPS CHERISH IT. AND NOW WE HAVE BEEN EXPERIENCING THE TRAGEDY AND THE LOSS OF LIFE THAT NOW SO MANY ACROSS THE COUNTRY HAVE ASSOCIATED WITH IT. NOW, I'M GOING TO TURN OVER TIME TO MY COLLEAGUES BECAUSE I'VE CERTAINLY BEEN ABLE TO EXPRESS A LOT OF MY VIEWS ABOUT THIS. BUT I WANT TO SAY JUST A COUPLE THINGS IN KICKING THIS OFF. AND THAT IS, I VIEW THINGS THROUGH THE LENS OF THE STORIES OF HEROISM, THE STORIES OF COURAGE, THE LIVES THAT WERE SAVED, THE PEOPLE THAT WERE AIRLIFTED, THE COAST GUARD THAT RESPONDED, THE SHERIFFS AND THE LOCAL LAW ENFORCEMENT THAT SHOWED UP, THE FIRST RESPONDERS THAT HELPED, THE STATE THAT WAS ON THE SCENE, THE CAMP COUNSELORS WHO SHOWED UP, THE CAMP DIRECTORS WHO GAVE THEIR LIVES. ALL OF THE PEOPLE WHO SHOWED UP AND THE SPIRIT AND THE STRONG FAITH OF A COMMUNITY BONDED TOGETHER BY FAITH THAT NOW ENDURES. AND  THAT TO ME IS THE ENDURING LEGACY. I TEND TO LOOK THROUGH THAT LENS BUT I DON'T THINK WE SHOULD MISS THIS MOMENT FOR THE PEOPLE OF THIS NATION TO UNDERSTAND, FROM THOSE OF US WHO UNDERSTAND TEXAS BEST, TO UNDERSTAND HOW HORRIFIC THIS TRULY WAS. WHEN I WENT ON THE SCENE AND SEVERAL OF US WERE THERE QUICKLY FOR A VARIETY OF REASON, WHICH WE'LL ALL HEAR ABOUT IN A MINUTE, BUT WHEN I WENT ON THE SCENE ON THE NIGHT OF JULY 4, AND THEN AGAIN ON THE 5TH AND TTHE 6TH AND THEN DRIVING OUT TO GO LOOK AT THE DAMAGE AND MEET WITH MY CONSTITUENTS AND MEET WITH PEOPLE AFFECTED, IT LOOKED LIKE AN F-5 TORNADO HAD JUST ROLLED DOWN THE RIVER. 100-YEAR-OLD TREES JUST LEVELED AND FLATTENED. HOUSES THAT WERE TOTALLY DESTROYED AND LIFTED OFF THE FOUNDATION. DEBRIS, PICKUP TRUCKS FULLY BURIED WITH A LITTLE PART OF IT STICKING OUT OF THE GROUND. AND OF COURSE AS WE'VE BEEN TALKING ABOUT, THE EXTRAORDINARY LOSS OF LIFE. WE ARE NOW AT WELL OVER 100 INDIVIDUALS WHO ARE KNOWN TO HAVE DECEASED, THAT ARE OFFICIALLY KNOWN IN KERR COUNTY, BUT MANY MORE EXPECTED. AND WELL OVER 100 INDIVIDUALS THAT ARE MISSING. AND OF COURSE NOW SOMEWHAT OF NOTE FOR THE ENTIRE COUNTRY ARE THESE WONDERFUL LITTLE GIRLS ASSOCIATED WITH CAMP MYSTIC. NOW, MY CHILDREN ARE 15 AND 14. THEY ARE RISING SOPHOMORES, SOPHOMORE AND FRESHMAN. MANY OF THEIR SCHOOLMATE, MANY OF THEIR FRIENDS GO TO CAMP MYSTIC OR GO TO ONE OF THE OTHER WONDERFUL CAMPS UP AND DOWN THIS AREA AND PART OF TEXAS. IT IS HARD TO PUT INTO WORDS HOW MUCH THIS IS A PART OF THE FABRIC OF OUR COMMUNITY IN CENTRAL TEXAS, BUT REALLY PARTICULARLY THE ENTIRE STATE OF TEXAS AND EVEN NATIONWIDE. WE HAD MANY OF OUR COLLEAGUES WHO WERE IMPACTED BY THIS. COLLEAGUE FROM GEORGIA, OTHER COLLEAGUES ACROSS THE ENTIRE NATION. I HAD COLLEAGUES FROM ALABAMA WHO WERE REACHING OUT BECAUSE THEY HAD CONSTITUENTS WHO WERE LOST. IT'S A WONDERFUL VACATION SPOT THAT WAS OBVIOUSLY TURNED ON ITS HEAD. BUT THE EXTRAORDINARY IMPACT IS GOING TO BE FELT FOR A LONG TIME. AND WE'RE GOING TO HAVE TO REBUILD AND WE'RE GOING TO HAVE TO TAKE THE TIME AND THE ENERGY NECESSARY TO DO IT. BUT IT IS, AS I BELIEVE -- I BELIEVE THE SPIRIT OF THE ENTIRE COMMUNITY THAT WILL ENDURE, AND AS I SAID EARLIER, AND I'LL TALK ABOUT MORE OF THIS LATER, IT IS FOR ME THE ENDURING IMAGE OF THOSE LITTLE GIRLS LEAVING THE CAMPS, SINGING HYMNS WHILE THEY SURVEYED THE DAMAGE AND THE PEOPLE THAT SHOWED UP WITH CROSSES AND SHOWED UP IN PRAYER GROUP, THE PEOPLE WHO SHOWED UP FROM CHURCHES, THE SAMARITANS, PURSE VOLUNTEERS WHO SHOWED UP WITHIN DAYS TO CLEAN OUT MUD AND THE PEOPLE WHO HAVE RALLIED AROUND THIS COMMUNITY AND THE PEOPLE ACROSS THIS COUNTRY WHO HAVE DONE SO THROUGH FAITH AND THROUGH BELIEF AND THROUGH THE POWER OF WHAT THESE LITTLE GIRLS REPRESENT. AND THE CHARM BRACELETS THAT THEY WEAR THAT ARE MADE BY THE LOCAL JEWELRY STORE, JAMES AVERY, THAT ARE A PART OF THE RICH HISTORY AND TRADITION. I COULD GO ON BUT MY COLLEAGUE FROM WEST TEXAS, HE HAS PERSONAL EXPERIENCE WITH THIS BECAUSE HIS FAMILY'S BEEN ASSOCIATED WITH THESE CAMPS FOR GENERATIONS. AND I'M GOING TO LET MY FRIEND, MR. PFLUGER, FILL IN A LITTLE BIT OF THE PERSONAL NATURE OF THIS AND THEN I LOOK FORWARD TO HEARING FROM THE REMAINDER MIGHT HAVE COLLEAGUES FROM THE TEXAS TELL GAITION. WITH THAT, I'LL -- DELEGATION. WITH THAT, I'LL YIELD TO MY FRIEND FROM TEXAS.",
