   {
    "member": "Chip Roy",
    "speaker_label": "MR. ROY",
    "transcript": "MR. SPEAKER, I RISE TODAY MOURNING THE LOSS OF LIFE IN THE STATE OF TEXAS BUT THAT TOUCHED PROFOUNDLY EVERYBODY ACROSS THIS GREAT COUNTRY. SO MANY PEOPLE WHO WERE VISITING THIS PART OF TEXAS. OBVIOUSLY WE HAVE BEEN STRUCK BY THE LOSS OF LIFE, PARTICULARLY FOR THOSE YOUNG GIRLS ASSOCIATED WITH CAMP MYSTIC. IT HAS BEEN GRUELING. IT WAS A ROUGH WEEK. A LOT OF DESTRUCTION. A LOT OF BEAUTIFUL PARTS OF OUR STATE THAT WERE DESTROYED. T WE WILL REBUILD. AND HERE'S THE THING THAT I WANT TO SAY. PEOPLE TALK ABOUT DESTRUCTION. WHAT WILL NOT BE DESTROYED IS THE SPIRIT OF THE PEOPLE OF TEXAS AND THE SPIRIT OF THE PEOPLE THAT THOSE CAMPS REPRESENT. THE SPIRIT OF THE LITTLE GIRLS WHO ARE ALREADY TALKING ABOUT WANTING TO GO BACK. THE SPIRIT OF THE PEOPLE ASSOCIATED WITH DICK EASTLON, THE CAMP DIRECTOR OF CAMP MYSTIC WHO GAVE HIS LIFE TRYING TO SAVE THE LITTLE GIRLS. THE SPIRIT OF JAMES WHO LOST THEIR -- JANE WHO LOST HER LIFESAVING FIVE LITTLE GIRLS. HER GUITAR WAS FOUND DOWN THE RIVER YESTERDAY. THE SPIRIT OF ALL OF THE LITTLE GIRLS THAT WERE RIDING IN THE BUS AS THEY LEFT CAMP MYSTIC, SINGING HYMNS, EXPRESSING THEIR FAITH AS THEY WERE LOOKING AT THE DESTRUCTION THEY COULDN'T POSSIBLY COMPREHEND AS THEY LEFT THAT CAMP. BUT THEY WERE STILL PUTTING THEIR FAITH IN THEIR LORD AND SAVOR -- SAVIOR. IF THERE IS ANYTHING WE CAN TAKE OUT OF THIS IT'S THAT SENSE OF COMMUNITY AND SENSE OF PRIDE WE HAVE IN KNOWING THAT WE WILL REBUILD AND COME TOGETHER, BUT THAT SENSE THAT WE KNOW THAT THE POWER OF THE CROSS THAT STANDS ON THE HILLS OVER THE CITY OF KERRVILLE, THE POWER OF THE FAITH OF THE PEOPLE OF TEXAS, THE POWER OF THE FAITH OF THE PEOPLE OF THIS NATION WHO HAVE RESPONDED, THE MILLIONS OF DOLLARS THAT HAVE COME IN TO THE COMMUNITY FOUNDATION OF THE HILL COUNTRY, $30 MILLION LAST WEEK, I THINK THAT NUMBER IS RISING, THANKS TO ALL OF YOU HERE IN THIS DELEGATION, MOST OF YOU HAVE REACHED OUT TO ME PERSONALLY AND MY FRIEND AND COLLEAGUES IN THIS DELEGATION. IT'S NOT JUST KERR COUNTY, IT'S THE STATE OF TEXAS. MANY OF MY COLLEAGUES HAVE BEEN AFFECTED ACROSS THE STATE. .. I CANNOT TELL YOU HOW PROUD I AM OF THE PEOPLE OF TEXAS AND THE PEOPLE OF KERR COUNTY TEXAS AND THE FIRST RESPONDERS WHO ARE TODAY BACK IN THE FLOODWATERS RESUMING THE SEARCH FOR THE MISSING. AND THERE IS STILL OVER 100 MISSING IN THAT PART OF OUR STATE. SO WITH THAT, MR. SPEAKER, I WOULD ASK FOR A MOMENT OF SILENCE.",
